<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela CANTV workers say wage talks going well.</title>
<headline>Venezuela CANTV workers say wage talks going well.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>On-going talks between labor and management at Venezuelan national telephone company CANTV over wage contracts &quot;are going rather well,&quot; Fetratel president Cruz Hernandez told Reuters.</p>
<p>Fetratel is a an umbrella labor group that gathers the 29 unions employed by CANTV. Hernandez said the group would hear a new, improved wage offer from CANTV on Wednesday for labor contracts in 1997 and 1998.</p>
<p>Hernandez played down the possibility of any strike, which had been threatened by one of Fetratel's unions in January. &quot;People are quite animated and prepared in the negotiations,&quot; he said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
